    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">How does CBT work?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">CBT is based on the idea that our thoughts, emotions, physical sensations and behaviours are all interconnected. Negative thought patterns can create a vicious cycle that perpetuates distress. By noticing and questioning these patterns, we work on the cycle together. CBT is usually structured and time-limited, often around 8 to 16 sessions. The length depends on the person and the subject.</p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary text-center">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Thoughts</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Identify automatic negative thoughts and cognitive distortions that fuel distress.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary text-center">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Emotions</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Understand how thoughts trigger emotional reactions and learn to regulate them.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary text-center">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Behaviours</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Gradually change avoidance patterns and develop healthier coping strategies.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-warm">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">What is CBT used for?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">CBT is one of the most researched psychotherapy approaches. It comes to the fore where there is a defined issue to work on and where thought patterns are keeping the picture in place. These are the areas we most often use CBT for at the centre.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-ink-muted">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Anxiety disorders and <a href="/en/blog/panic-attack-symptoms.html" class="text-primary underline hover:no-underline">panic attacks</a></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Obsessive thoughts and repeated checking behaviour</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span><a href="/en/blog/what-is-depression.html" class="text-primary underline hover:no-underline">Low mood</a> and loss of motivation</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span><a href="/en/blog/coping-with-exam-anxiety.html" class="text-primary underline hover:no-underline">Exam anxiety</a> and performance anxiety</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Sleep difficulties and procrastination</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">How many sessions does CBT take?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">CBT is usually short-term work. When focused on a defined issue, most processes are completed within 8–20 sessions. Sessions last 45 minutes and are usually weekly.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">No fixed number is given at the outset. Once it is clear what we are working on, we agree an approximate frame together.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-warm">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">Is there homework between sessions?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Because CBT is structured, some things are tried between sessions. Usually that means noticing a thought and writing it down, or approaching an avoided situation in small steps.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">These are experiments, not exams. When they are not done, that too becomes something to talk about — what got in the way often says something useful about the work itself.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
